    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11850" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπεναντίον</span></b> , Adv.
		= foreg., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ἀ.</span> (sc.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χώρα</span>) the <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>opposite</i> shore, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς τὴν ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.55
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				7.6.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				19.38
			</span></i>: c. dat., <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>UP</u>
				1.9
			</span></i>: c. gen., <i>from before,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ca.</u>
				6.4
			</span></i>: Geom., of angles, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ἀ.
			γωνία</span> the <i>opposite</i> angle, <i><span class="en">
				Euc.
				1.16
			</span></i>, al.; of sides of a figure, <i><span class="en">
				Archim.
				<u>Aequil.</u>
				2.1
			</span></i>, hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπεναντίος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Procop.
				<u>Aed.</u>
				1.11
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίως</span>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Nigr.</u>
				36
			</span></i>.</div>
